cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HAR2Client, please cite it as below."
title: "HAR2Client: a benchmark for turning recorded HTTP traffic into working API clients"
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohitGoyal09/har2client"
authors:
  - family-names: "Goyal"
    given-names: "Mohit"
    email: "goel0632@gmail.com"
  - family-names: "Bhattacharya"
    given-names: "Ananya"
    email: "bhattacharya.ananya004@gmail.com"
abstract: >-
  HAR2Client grades a model on one skill: given recorded HTTP traffic of an
  API and a goal, write a client that works on a fresh copy of that API.
  It runs the client against a fresh fake server with hidden tests and uses
  no LLM judge. It also holds a code-repair case (update an old client after
  the API changed) and a reinforcement learning environment.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - HAR
  - API client
  - code generation
  - reinforcement learning environment
